{"title":"ITest","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The title of this article has been capitalized due to technical restrictions. The correct title should be '</i><b>iTest'</b><i>.</i></dd></dl>\n<p>The <b>iTest</b> (formerly the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_High_School_Internet_Mathematics_Competition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"American High School Internet Mathematics Competition\">American High School Internet Mathematics Competition</a>) is a team-based math competition for high school students.  The difficulty in the test is varied, ranging from simple arithmetic problems to complex Olympiad problems.  Winning teams earn recent technology prizes like a video game console of their choice.\n</p>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:10px;float:right;margin:10px;background:#fff;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;text-align:center;background:#ccf;\"><b>iTest</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Region</b>: USA\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Type</b>: Multiple Choice, Free Response, Proof\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Competition_ratings\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Competition ratings\">Difficulty</a></b>: 1-8\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Difficulty Breakdown:</b>\n<p><u>MC Questions</u>: 1-4.5<br /><u>FR Questions (Earlier)</u>: 1-4.5<br /><u>FR Questions (Later)</u>: 4-8\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Structure\">Structure</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Structure\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The iTest covers traditional high school math concepts, including <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">algebra</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>, pre-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">calculus</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic\" title=\"Logic\">logic</a>.  Graphing calculators are allowed, but computers are not allowed.\n</p><p>Prior to 2008, the iTest has multiple choice, free response, and an \"Ultimate\" question.  In the multiple choice questions, there is 1 choice on the first problem, 2 choices on the second problem, and so on.  The \"Ultimate\" question is a series of 10 questions where each question requires the answer of a previous problem, much like the relay questions of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ARML\">ARML</a>.  There were also 4 tiebreaker proof questions.\n</p><p>In the 2008 iTest, there are 100 free response questions with a storyline attached that connects most of the problems.  Unlike previous years, ties will solely be broken by submission time.\n</p><p>The 2007 and 2008 iTest also have a Tournament of Champions, a series of harder free response problems.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Logos\">Logos</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Logos\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Itest2007.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"2007 logo.\"><img alt=\"2007 logo.\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fa/Itest2007.jpg/120px-Itest2007.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"36\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fa/Itest2007.jpg/180px-Itest2007.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fa/Itest2007.jpg/240px-Itest2007.jpg 2x\" /></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">2007 logo.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Itest2006.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"2006 logo.\"><img alt=\"2006 logo.\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/28/Itest2006.jpg/120px-Itest2006.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"54\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/28/Itest2006.jpg/180px-Itest2006.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/28/Itest2006.jpg 2x\" /></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">2006 logo.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:ITest2005.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"2005 logo.\"><img alt=\"2005 logo.\" src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/18/ITest2005.gif/120px-ITest2005.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/18/ITest2005.gif/180px-ITest2005.gif 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/18/ITest2005.gif 2x\" /></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">2005 logo.</div>\n\t\t</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ITest_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"ITest Problems and Solutions\">iTest Problems and Solutions</a> on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPSWiki\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPSWiki\">AoPSWiki</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3435\">AoPS Community</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141303\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 656/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 161/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2026/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.967      1 -total\n 62.26%    9.318      1 Template:Contest_Info\n 36.91%    5.524      1 Template:Title_restriction\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5159:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141303 and revision id 243781. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}